        notes: 'Sloane MS 3188 holds Dee’s conferences with angels from 22 December 1581, in five books, on ff. 4r–108r; ff. 109r–169v are William Shippen’s notes in cipher. The British Library’s record ends the conferences on 30 May 1583, Christopher Whitby’s thesis of 1982 on 23 May. Peterson’s edition of the fifth book opens on 23 March 1583 and has sessions headed 26 March, the day Wikipedia gives for Kelley’s first sight of the letters; what Dee wrote that day is not quoted in the sources used here, so the dated table of 6 May stands as the first witness. Elias Ashmole later made a fair copy of these books, now Sloane MS 3677. Kelley had begun to work with Dee in 1582; the letters belong to 1583.',
